# OpenCode's grep/glob tools shell out to ripgrep. Its resolution order is
# which("rg") -> $HOME/.cache/opencode/bin/rg -> download from GitHub releases.
# The download verifies nothing but a non-zero byte length, and the adapter gives
# each run a fresh HOME, so the cache is always cold and every review would fetch
# and exec an unverified binary. Installing this pinned, checksum-verified copy on
# PATH short-circuits at the first step.
#
# Keep the version equal to the one the pinned opencode-ai would fetch, so the
# reviewer runs the ripgrep OpenCode was tested against. The version here and the
# port of the artifact URL are bound to opencode-ai's downloads; refresh steps,
# including how to observe the version opencode would fetch, live in
# ai-review/images/SUPPLY_CHAIN.md.
version=15.1.0
url=https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/releases/download/15.1.0/ripgrep-15.1.0-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz
sha256=1c9297be4a084eea7ecaedf93eb03d058d6faae29bbc57ecdaf5063921491599
